  "notes": "Sub-objective ids (1.1.a, 1.1.b, ...) are assigned by this site in the order the document prints the bullets, reading each objective's columns one after another (the whole first column top to bottom, then the second, then the third). \"details\" holds every deeper line, flattened as \"Parent > child\", with each child listed right after its parent. A column that begins with dash or circle lines continues the last bullet (or dash line) of the column before it: in 1.4 the third column (Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) to Wildcard) continues \"Certificates\"; in 2.1 the second column (Blackmail to War) continues \"Motivations\"; in 3.1 the second column's first line (Software-defined networking (SDN)) continues the list under \"Physical isolation\"; in 3.2 \"Protocol (EAP)\" at the top of the second column finishes \"Extensible Authentication\"; in 3.3 \"Private\" and \"Critical\" continue \"Data classifications\" and the third column (Encryption to Permission restrictions) continues \"Methods to secure data\"; in 4.6 \"Discretionary\" at the top of the second column continues \"Access controls\"; in 4.7 the third column (Single point of failure, Technical debt, Ongoing supportability) continues \"Other considerations\"; in 4.8 the third column (Legal hold to E-discovery) continues \"Digital forensics\"; in 5.1 \"Government entities\" and \"Centralized/decentralized\" at the top of the third column continue \"Types of governance structures\"; in 5.4 the third column (Data subject to Right to be forgotten) continues \"Privacy\". Wrapped lines are joined with one space, including \"Extensible Authentication Protocol (EAP)\" in 3.2, which wraps across two columns and is written as \"Port security > Extensible Authentication Protocol (EAP)\". In 3.1 the document prints \"Physical isolation\" as a dash line, \"Air-gapped\" one level deeper, then \"Logical segmentation\" as a circle line, and the second column opens with the circle line \"Software-defined networking (SDN)\"; all three are written under \"Physical isolation\" (\"Physical isolation > Air-gapped\", \"Physical isolation > Logical segmentation\", \"Physical isolation > Software-defined networking (SDN)\"). In 4.7 the line \"and access\" is printed with its own dash but is the end of \"Enabling/disabling services\", so it is joined as one detail, \"Enabling/disabling services and access\". Wording, capitals, and spacing are as the document prints them, including \"Humanand non-human-readable\" in 3.3 (the document has no space after \"Human\") and \"Universal Resource Locator (URL) scanning\" in 4.5; the stray leading spaces the document prints before a few lines in 4.1 and 4.4 are left out. No character was changed.",
